// A known limitation (the CIL frontend translation, §12.5, `engine:alias-rule`): an object
// stored into its own field is a cycle, and the index's aliasing rule summarizes only the
// paths the program stores through. `b.o = b; return b.o` returns `b`, whose `.o` is `b`
// again, so `return.o <- b` holds; the index does not derive it. `cil:taint` meets this in
// `Exec.Obj::ObjectField`; its known-miss file points here. `flowy_tests.rs` skips this file
// until the aliasing rule covers cycles.
def F(b): 1
where summaries [return.o <- b]
{
start:
  b.o = b;
  t = b.o;
  return t;
}
